WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.080
A made up case.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.040
Nandini is a district collector,

3
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.800
so her phone is never really

4
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.010
off. At two a.m., it rings.

5
00:00:09.684 --> 00:00:11.944
The dam engineer upstream says

6
00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:13.324
heavy rain has filled the

7
00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:16.304
reservoir. At five a.m., the

8
00:00:16.304 --> 00:00:17.634
gates must open.

9
00:00:18.181 --> 00:00:20.601
Four villages sit low on the

10
00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.041
riverbank, and the rain has not

11
00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:24.011
stopped.

12
00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:25.494
The dilemma:

13
00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:27.454
who does she wake first, and

14
00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:29.584
what does she order before dawn?

15
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.277
Option A:

16
00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:32.997
wait for morning and confirmed

17
00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:35.497
numbers. Option B:

18
00:00:35.497 --> 00:00:37.477
sound every alarm at once.

19
00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:38.737
Option C:

20
00:00:38.737 --> 00:00:39.957
call the engineer back for

21
00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.237
timings, wake her disaster team,

22
00:00:42.237 --> 00:00:43.477
and move the four villages

23
00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:46.227
first. Pause here, and choose.

24
00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:49.401
Option A waits for certainty.

25
00:00:49.401 --> 00:00:50.701
But the guidelines treat

26
00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:53.281
evacuation as a precaution, done

27
00:00:53.281 --> 00:00:54.851
before the water comes.

28
00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.290
Option B has urgency but no

29
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.330
order. Each department's role

30
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.900
should be fixed beforehand.

31
00:01:02.781 --> 00:01:04.941
Option C uses her office.

32
00:01:04.941 --> 00:01:06.281
The collector chairs the

33
00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:07.661
District Disaster Management

34
00:01:07.661 --> 00:01:09.721
Authority, and can direct

35
00:01:09.721 --> 00:01:11.961
departments, control traffic and

36
00:01:11.961 --> 00:01:13.111
arrange shelter.

37
00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:15.561
A sound answer confirms the

38
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:17.941
warning, wakes the right people,

39
00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:20.101
moves the low villages first,

40
00:01:20.101 --> 00:01:22.091
and keeps everyone informed.

41
00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:24.619
For GS4 and GS3:

42
00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:27.179
act early on a credible warning,

43
00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:28.099
in order.

44
00:01:28.099 --> 00:01:31.229
The morning can be too late.

45
00:01:31.982 --> 00:01:34.442
By sunrise the river was high.

46
00:01:34.442 --> 00:01:36.482
The villages were quiet;

47
00:01:36.482 --> 00:01:38.222
their people were already on

48
00:01:38.222 --> 00:01:39.412
higher ground.
